CONTINUE_REFACTORING

Even though all of the Flink APIs still legitimately reference “Job…” (JobID, JobGraph, JobResult, JobManagerOptions, etc.), our own test code still has three remaining “job” identifiers that should be renamed to “stream”:

1) In every test method we capture the returned JobResult into a local named  

   ```java
   JobResult jobResult = …;
   ```  

   Rename those locals (and all subsequent references) to something like:  

   ```java
   JobResult streamResult = flinkCluster.requestJobResult(streamId).get();
   assertThat(streamResult.getSerializedThrowable()).isEmpty();
   ```

2) The private helper method’s signature still reads  

   ```java
   private void triggerJMFailover(JobID jobId) { … }
   ```  

   Change the parameter name to `streamId` (and update its two usages inside):  

   ```java
   private void triggerJMFailover(JobID streamId) throws Exception {
       highAvailabilityServices.revokeJobMasterLeadership(streamId).get();
       highAvailabilityServices.grantJobMasterLeadership(streamId);
   }
   ```

3) Update all calls to `triggerJMFailover(...)` so that the argument name matches, e.g.  

   ```java
   triggerJMFailover(streamId);
   ```

With those three renames, there will be no remaining occurrences of our own “job…” identifiers in the test code.

